WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.762
information and both eyes.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.932
And glasses use lenses to help
focus light on the retina.

00:00:05.507 --> 00:00:08.268
That is different from
controlling how much light enters.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.726
Earlier you correctly said a transmitted
ray might not emerge from glass.

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:14.858
What special phenomenon could occur

00:00:14.858 --> 00:00:15.458
instead?

00:00:16.251 --> 00:00:18.103
Total internal reflection.

00:00:18.688 --> 00:00:22.330
But I need two conditions, not
just a dramatic bouncing arrow.

00:00:22.988 --> 00:00:23.606
Name them.

00:00:24.477 --> 00:00:27.574
Light must travel from a higher
refractive index medium towards

00:00:27.575 --> 00:00:29.414
a lower refractive index medium.

00:00:29.992 --> 00:00:32.525
Its angle of incidence must
be greater than the critical

00:00:32.525 --> 00:00:34.220
angle measured from the normal.

00:00:34.923 --> 00:00:35.614
Excellent.

00:00:36.248 --> 00:00:39.693
At the critical angle, the refracted
ray would run along the boundary.

00:00:39.946 --> 00:00:43.614
Above it, ideal total
internal reflection occurs.

00:00:43.964 --> 00:00:47.618
Below it, some light can be
refracted out as well as reflected.

00:00:48.324 --> 00:00:51.660
So an optical fiber does not
need glass surrounded by air.

00:00:52.014 --> 00:00:55.401
It can have a higher index
core and lower index cladding.

00:00:56.211 --> 00:00:57.045
Exactly.

00:00:57.426 --> 00:01:01.803
Guided light carries information through
fibers, including communication links.

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:04.447
Some medical instruments also use fibers.

00:01:04.851 --> 00:01:09.744
Real fibers have losses and light travels
more slowly in glass than in a vacuum.

00:01:10.497 --> 00:01:13.439
I should not write that fiber
internet travels through glass

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.915
at the vacuum speed with zero

00:01:14.923 --> 00:01:15.824
losses forever.

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:17.220
Correct.

00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:20.778
Nor should you claim every ray
entering a fiber will be guided.

00:01:21.104 --> 00:01:23.306
The geometry and entry conditions matter.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.029
Our schematic shows a suitable path,
not a promise about every direction

00:01:28.362 --> 00:01:29.301
Rescue round.

00:01:29.642 --> 00:01:32.615
A ray meets a mirror at
twenty degrees to the surface.

00:01:32.984 --> 00:01:34.640
What is the angle of reflection?

00:01:35.398 --> 00:01:39.414
Seventy degrees, because the angle of
incidence is measured from the normal.

00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:42.041
Twenty plus seventy makes ninety.

00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:43.112
Good.

00:01:43.429 --> 00:01:45.347
Light enters glass along the normal.

00:01:45.668 --> 00:01:46.740
Does it change speed?

00:01:46.881 --> 00:01:48.039
Does it change direction?

00:01:48.825 --> 00:01:52.929
Its speed decreases, but it does not
bend away from its original direction.

00:01:53.402 --> 00:01:56.730
A speed change does not guarantee
bending at normal incidence.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:01.250
Third, does a red filter
make blue light turn red?

00:02:01.972 --> 00:02:02.325
No.

00:02:02.723 --> 00:02:04.855
It selectively transmits wavelengths.

00:02:05.338 --> 00:02:09.404
With only blue light arriving, a
suitable red filter transmits little

00:02:09.482 --> 00:02:11.164
rather than creating red light.

00:02:11.881 --> 00:02:15.653
Finally, name the eye's two
controls and the two conditions

00:02:15.665 --> 00:02:17.495
for total internal reflection.

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:20.950
Iris controls pupil size and light entry.

00:02:21.238 --> 00:02:23.281
Lens curvature controls focus.

00:02:23.823 --> 00:02:27.759
Total internal reflection needs
travel from higher to lower refractive

00:02:27.762 --> 00:02:31.208
index and an incidence angle
greater than the critical angle.

00:02:31.958 --> 00:02:37.477
Our imaginary exam marks can unpack their
suitcases, draw normals first, label

00:02:37.478 --> 00:02:42.294
arrows, separate real rays from virtual
extensions, and explain the mechanism.

00:02:42.838 --> 00:02:45.759
A careful diagram can
rescue a whole explanation
